A union directory read continues below without a console report.

getdirentries moves an open directory of a union mount to the directory below it once the upper one is read. The first 48
moves of a boot were printed ("union readdir: <name> lookup 0 step 0 error 0"), a measurement that has its answer: of the 240
lines of five sheng boots, 237 report a move that happened and 3 report System/Library/dyld, which has no directory below. A
kernel printf is written by the calling thread, to the log and through the console ring to the consoles; with vc-text=1 that
includes the text drawn on the boot framebuffer, and these lines come while launchd and the first daemons list their
directories. The report is removed: the function is the original one again plus the end of directory rule of
native-union-readdir-eof.patch, which stays.
Requires native-union-readdir-eof.patch.

